        "answer": {
          "short": "i $\\frac{12}{25}$\n\nii $\\frac{8}{15}$",
          "worked": "The spheres may be drawn red then blue, or blue then red. Add the probabilities of these two orders.\n\ni With replacement:\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{one red and one blue})&=\\frac{6}{10}\\times\\frac{4}{10}+\\frac{4}{10}\\times\\frac{6}{10}\\\\P(\\text{one red and one blue})&=\\frac{12}{25}\\end{align*}$$\nii Without replacement:\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{one red and one blue})&=\\frac{6}{10}\\times\\frac{4}{9}+\\frac{4}{10}\\times\\frac{6}{9}\\\\P(\\text{one red and one blue})&=\\frac{8}{15}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
